# PRODUCTION-ONLY GATE FOR THE INTERIM LANDING PAGE
#
# Marty asked to stop the public site serving messaging that no longer matches
# where the company is. These rules send every interior page back to the landing
# page at / -- but ONLY on the live public domains.
#
# securelogic.netlify.app is deliberately NOT listed, so the whole site stays
# browsable there for internal review while the rebuild continues.
#
# DOMAINS
#   genesis360.com is the primary domain. Both apex and www are listed.
#
#   securelogicusa.com is kept here too. It is expected to redirect to
#   genesis360.com at the registrar, in which case these rules never fire for it
#   -- traffic lands on genesis360.com before Netlify sees it. They cost nothing
#   and they are the safety net for the case where securelogicusa.com resolves
#   to this Netlify site directly instead of being redirected upstream. If that
#   ever changes, do not delete them without checking where its DNS points.
#
# This file is dormant until a listed domain actually points at Netlify. It
# switches itself on at DNS cutover with no redeploy needed.
#
# TO PUT THE FULL SITE BACK LIVE: delete this file, then copy
# src/pages/home-full.astro back over src/pages/index.astro. Nothing else
# changes, because nothing was ever removed -- all 43 pages still build on every
# deploy.
#
# MECHANICS
#   * A full URL in the left column is how Netlify scopes a rule to one host. A
#     bare path like /ag/* would match every domain, including netlify.app,
#     which is exactly what we are avoiding here.
#   * 302, not 301. A 301 is cached hard by browsers and would keep sending
#     people to the landing page for weeks after relaunch.
#   * The trailing ! forces the rule to win over the real page that exists at
#     that path. Without it Netlify just serves the page and never redirects.
#   * Each section is listed twice per host, with and without the splat, because
#     /ag/* does not reliably match a bare /ag.
#   * /privacy-policy is intentionally absent -- legal page, no product
#     messaging, and the Facebook and Instagram profiles link to it.
#
# UNTESTABLE LOCALLY. Host-scoped rules cannot fire locally or on netlify.app.
# Verify with curl against www.genesis360.com after each deploy (see TASKS.md).
#
# OPEN PAGES (exceptions to the gate)
#   Netlify takes the FIRST matching rule, so a page is opened by putting a
#   more specific 200! rewrite-to-itself ABOVE the section splat that would
#   otherwise catch it. The ! is needed because without it Netlify would treat
#   the rule as shadowed by the real file and fall through to the 302 below.
#   Open pages must also render the minimal header/footer, or their nav links
#   lead straight back into the gate -- see src/data/launch-gate.ts.
#
#   2026-09-16  /ag/hogs-livestock/  opened for the hog page launch.
#   2026-09-16  /ag and /ag/* forward to the hog page instead of / (see # ag).

